  "hypothesis": "A contiguous byte matrix should make mismatch updates over swapped vertices inexpensive. Combining it with the existing identity check, unrolled degree reductions, and degree-multiset rejection may let incremental mismatch tracking reduce the cost of testing each remaining Heap permutation.",
